  "RQ1 orientation": "Autonomous cyber-threat defense",
  "RQ2 architecture": "Distributed, tool-augmented, explainable multi-agent system: Safety and Security Agent (SSA), Personalized Support Agent (PSA), Contextualizer Agent (CA), and Solver Agent (SA); shared explainable reasoning layer",
  "RQ2 llm_used": "LLaMA2-7B, LLaMA2-13B, LLaMA3-8B; fine-tuned DistilBERT intent recognizer, DeBERTa and RoBERTa comparisons; GPT-4 references and DeepSeek judge",
  "RQ2 adaptation": "Prompt engineering and RAG for SSA; fine-tuned DistilBERT, pretrained ML/DL tools, and continual learning through federated, transfer, and split learning",
  "RQ3 autonomy_level": "Agents continuously monitor battery conditions, detect faults and intrusions, dynamically invoke diagnostic and explainability tools, and generate responses; support agents formalize, contextualize, and solve optimization requests",
  "RQ3 hitl": "Application layer provides decision oversight and feedback; domain experts verify and annotate evaluation references and assess generated responses",
